    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d399">

                <pb facs="1170" n="1164" sameAs="frus:frus1894app2/pg1164"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Frelinghuysen to
                        Mr. Daggett.</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No 19.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1883-03-02"><hi rendition="#italic">March 2,
                        1883</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Your dispatch of the 12th ultimo, No. 49,
                    reporting the peaceful crowning of the King and Queen of the Hawaiian Islands at
                    noon of that day has been received.</p>
                <p>The present is a fitting occasion to express anew the assurances of the good will
                    we bear to the Hawaiian Government and people. We have also especial pleasure in
                    learning that, as reported in your No. 41 of the 10th ultimo, two of our
                    national vessels arrived at Honolulu in season for His Majesty’s coronation.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Fred’k T.
                    Frelinghuysen.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
